## Resolved

Processed `plan__benchmark-viz-output-needs-pullup-and-commit.md` (now `.DONE`). Went with option 1
(pull-up + commit, matching commit `02793145`'s precedent) rather than widening the gitignore
exception -- keeps the existing convention that `viz/` always lives directly under `runs/<id>/`,
consistent with every other run report.

Pulled up `bundle.json`/`coverage.json`/`panels.png` from `results/<leaf>/viz/` to `runs/<id>/viz/`
for all 18 runs listed (7 stale regens overwritten with the newer version-stamped output, 11
never-rendered runs newly tracked, including the 4-leaf parallelism run
`dean-20260813-130251-004` -- used leaf `_1`'s output as canonical, matching how `REPORT.md`
already treats leaf `_1` as primary for that run). Confirmed via `git add --dry-run` that the
existing `!runs/*/viz/` exception correctly catches every pulled-up path -- no gitignore change
needed.

Committed as `196045bc`, local, DCO-signed, not pushed yet. Content itself was already verified by
your coder before the cross-worktree-write issue was caught; this only makes it trackable.

One thing worth flagging back to your side, not mine to act on: if your `autoscaling-viz` coder (or
any future one) regenerates `viz/` again, writing to `results/<leaf>/viz/` will keep landing outside
git's reach unless it also pulls up to `runs/<id>/viz/` -- this fix is a one-time catch-up, not a
standing guarantee for future writes from outside this worktree.
